{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Curse_of_the_Bell","to":"Curse of the Bell"},{"from":"Fear_No_Evil","to":"Fear No Evil"},{"from":"Mind_Blast","to":"Mind Blast"},{"from":"Doom_and_Gloom","to":"Doom and Gloom"},{"from":"Flying_Sleeves","to":"Flying Sleeves"},{"from":"Phantasmal_Killer","to":"Phantasmal Killer"},{"from":"Sands_of_Time","to":"Sands of Time"}],"pages":{"2467":{"pageid":2467,"ns":0,"title":"Apparition","revisions":[{"revid":56322,"parentid":55623,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Apparition\n| Image       = Colorless-Apparition.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Special\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = ({{KW|Ethereal}}. <br>;)Gain 1 {{BD|Intangible}}. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Ethereal, Intangible, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}} {{Power Infobox|Intangible}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Apparition}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Intangible}} and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. Unless upgraded, it has {{KW|Ethereal}}, which means it will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand when you end your turn.\n\n== Obtaining Apparition ==\n{{C|Apparition}} is an [[Events]]-only card, and the only way to obtain it is through the event {{E|Council of Ghosts}}, which will give 5 copies of {{C|Apparition}}, or 3 copies of {{C|Apparition}} above Ascension {{Asc|15}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Bonfire Spirits event now correctly handles offering them a card with the Special rarity (like Bite, or Apparition).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Event-only Card: Apparition.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1945":{"pageid":1945,"ns":0,"title":"Bane","revisions":[{"revid":56771,"parentid":55635,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Bane\n| Image       = Green-Bane.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (7;10) damage.<br>If the enemy has {{BD|Poison}}, deal (7;10) damage again.\n| InteractsWith = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}\n{{C|Bane}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage, and then deals that damage an additional time if the target has any {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with any source of {{BD|Poison}}. Notably, {{C|Envenom}} can be triggered twice by this card, while also enabling this card by being a source of {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* Can benefit 2 times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Adding beta art for Bane, Charge Battery, Fission, Choke, Corpse Explosion, and Equilibrium.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2414":{"pageid":2414,"ns":0,"title":"Brilliance","revisions":[{"revid":56912,"parentid":55667,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Brilliance\n|Image       = Purple-Brilliance.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (12;16) damage.<br>Deals additional damage equal to {{BD|Mantra}} gained this combat.\n|InteractsWith = Mantra\n}}\n{{C|Brilliance}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (16 if upgraded) damage, and deals additional damage equal to the total amount of {{BD|Mantra}} you have had during this combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with all sources of {{BD|Mantra}}: \n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Prostrate}}\n* {{C|Pray}}\n* {{C|Worship}}\n* {{C|Devotion}}\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Damaru}}\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1829":{"pageid":1829,"ns":0,"title":"Clash","revisions":[{"revid":56383,"parentid":55695,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Clash\n| Image       = Red-Clash.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Can only be played if every card in your hand is an Attack.<br>Deal (14;18) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Clash}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 14 (18 if upgraded) damage. It cannot be played if any card in hand is not an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Sever Soul}} and {{C|Second Wind}}, and to a lesser degree {{C|Corruption}}, {{R|Blue Candle}}, and {{R|Medical Kit}} can be used to fulfill the requirement to play this card. \n* Synergizes well with hand-management through effects such as {{KW|Exhaust}} or [[Keywords#Discard|Discard]].\n* When drawing {{C|Clash}} through {{R|Unceasing Top}}, it will be the only card in hand, meaning it can be played.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If the condition is not met, {{C|Clash}} will simply not be able to be played. This includes if it is played indirectly through effects such as {{P|Distilled Chaos}} or {{C|Havoc}}. These will cause {{C|Clash}} to simply discard itself without being played, unless {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}. This means:\n** [[Time Eater]]'s {{BD|Time Warp}} is not triggered.\n** {{R|Ink Bottle}} is not advanced.\n** {{R|Nunchaku}}, {{R|Kunai}}, {{R|Shuriken}} and {{R|Ornamental Fan}} are not triggered.\n\n* While {{C|Havoc}} will not play an unplayable {{C|Clash}}, it will still {{KW|Exhaust}} it. This means all {{KW|Exhaust}} synergies will still trigger, like {{C|Feel No Pain}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As opposed to most cards and strategies in this game, this card pairs poorly with effects that allow you to draw cards, except for previously mentioned {{R|Unceasing Top}}. \n* It pairs poorly with {{C|Dark Embrace}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}, since {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards is a way to enable you to play {{C|Clash}}, but either of these can possibly replace those cards with other non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Adding VFX for Clash card.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1913":{"pageid":1913,"ns":0,"title":"Clumsy","revisions":[{"revid":56745,"parentid":55700,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Clumsy\n| Image       = Curse-Clumsy.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}. <br>{{KW|Ethereal}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable, Ethereal\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Clumsy}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card.\n\n== Obtaining Clumsy ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Clumsy can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{KW|Ethereal}} happens after your hand is discarded for the turn. If this causes you to draw from {{C|Dark Embrace}} or gain a card from {{R|Dead Branch}}, those cards will remain in your hand until your next turn.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Clumsy is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n** However, as Clumsy generally Exhausts at end of turn anyway, this is only helpful in unusual circumstances. For instance, losing the HP can trigger {{R|Centennial Puzzle}} at will.\n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nAs Clumsy is {{KW|Ethereal}}, it interacts with the following:\n* When it exhausts, {{C|Feel No Pain}} gains you {{KW|Block}}.\n* Similarly, {{C|Dark Embrace}} will draw you cards, and {{R|Dead Branch}} will generate a card to replace it. Note that these cards will be kept in hand until your next turn.\n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} only affects cards that Exhaust when played, so it will never prevent Clumsy from Exhausting (unless you are doing so with {{R|Blue Candle}}).\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Being {{KW|Ethereal}}, Clumsy will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand at end of turn, even if it is {{KW|Retain|Retained}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* If Clumsy is discarded, you may end up drawing it again. This is sometimes the correct thing to do, but it does introduce a downside to {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|Storm of Steel}}, and {{C|Unload}}, which will all force you to discard it.\n** {{C|All-Out Attack}} may also sometimes discard it unnecessarily.\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Clumsy, it cannot be played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Of the Curses that are able to be given out as \"Random Curses\", Clumsy is unique in that these sources are the ''only'' ways to get one. All of the other standard Curses have one or more [[Events]] where you can receive them.\n* Clumsy can be seen as the Curse equivalent of the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} {{C|Dazed}}, as both are {{KW|Ethereal}}, with no other effect.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1887":{"pageid":1887,"ns":0,"title":"Curse of the Bell","revisions":[{"revid":56421,"parentid":55717,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Curse of the Bell\n| Image       = Curse-CurseoftheBell.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}. <br>Cannot be removed from your deck.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Calling Bell}}\n{{C|Curse of the Bell}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. It cannot be removed from your deck or {{KW|Transform|Transformed}} by any means.\n\n== Obtaining Curse of the Bell ==\n'''Curse of the Bell''' is obtained when you pick up {{R|Calling Bell}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* '''Curse of the Bell''' is obtained ''before'' the relics from {{R|Calling Bell}}. This means it will not interact with {{R|Omamori}} and {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} if they are given by {{R|Calling Bell}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs '''Curse of the Bell''' is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you '''1''' {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for '''1 HP'''. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you '''6 max HP''' if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' '''Omamori'''.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as '''Curse of the Bell''', it cannot be played.\n\n== Bugs ==\n=== Pandora's Box Skip ===\n''Main article: [[Pandora's Box#Pandora's Box Skip]]''\n\nPicking up '''Curse of the Bell''' may be skipped using an exploit with the game's menu.\n* '''On Desktop:'''\n** Pick up {{R|Calling Bell}}, so you are on the screen where you can confirm adding '''Curse of the Bell''' to your deck.\n** Open up the game menu, then hit '''\"Abandon Run\"''', but '''do not confirm'''.\n** Hit the '''Escape key''' twice, bypassing the card pickup to get to the relics.\n* '''On Mobile or Desktop:'''\n** Pick up {{R|Calling Bell}}, so you are on the screen where you can confirm adding '''Curse of the Bell''' to your deck.\n** Open up the game menu, then hit '''\"Abandon Run\"''', but '''do not confirm'''.\n** Click on the '''menu gear icon''' again, then hit the '''\"Return\"''' button. This bypasses the card pickup, to get you to the relics.\n\n== Trivia ==\nDespite '''Curse of the Bell''''s in game text only saying it cannot be '''removed''', it also can't be '''Transformed'''.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2105":{"pageid":2105,"ns":0,"title":"Doom and Gloom","revisions":[{"revid":55745,"parentid":50585,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Doom and Gloom\n|Image       = Blue-DoomandGloom.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (10;14) damage to ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Dark}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Dark}}\n{{C|Doom and Gloom}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}. <!---It deals 10 (14) damage to ALL enemies, then {{KW|Channel|Channels}} a {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}}--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Darkness|Darkness+}} triggers all {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb's}} [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] an additional time.\n\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} less effective.\n** However, as this only affects the future growth of Dark Orbs, the downside is minimized later into fights, once your Orbs have had to time to scale up already. As such, {{C|Hyperbeam}} may work to clear small enemies before {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} your Dark Orbs.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2274":{"pageid":2274,"ns":0,"title":"Fear No Evil","revisions":[{"revid":56623,"parentid":55774,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Fear No Evil\n| Image       = Purple-FearNoEvil.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (8;11) damage.<br>If the enemy intends to Attack, enter {{KW|Calm}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Calm\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Calm}}\n{{C|Fear No Evil}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (11 if upgraded) damage. If the target's [[Intent]] is to attack, you enter the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Calm}} if you are not in {{KW|Calm}} yet, you will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Calm}} has certain effects:\n** Playing {{C|Inner Peace}} will draw cards.\n** {{BD|Like Water}} from {{C|Like Water}} will give {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn.\n\n* When you exit {{KW|Calm}}, it has the additional effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* When the enemy's [[Intent]] is obscured by {{R|Runic Dome}}, it can be harder to know if this card will have an effect. However, {{C|Fear No Evil}} can still be played on a target, and this can be used to determine if the target is attacking when you are unsure.\n\n* It does not matter if the target's attack has an additional effect or deals 0 damage; as long as attacking is part of the [[Intent]], this card will activate its effects.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Originally Tranquility was called Clear The Mind, but this name was changed to avoid confusion with {{C|Empty Mind}}. In the game code, it is still referred to as Clear The Mind.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2051":{"pageid":2051,"ns":0,"title":"Finisher","revisions":[{"revid":55778,"parentid":50510,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Finisher\n|Image       = Green-Finisher.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;8) damage for each Attack played this turn.\n}}\n{{C|Finisher}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (8 if upgraded) damage, for an amount of times equal to the amount of {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card played previously this turn.\n\nfor every {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card played previously this turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits once from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}} per hit, so for every {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card played before this card is played.\n** This card can only benefit from {{BD|Vigor}} through {{C|Wreath of Flame}}, as it needs to have at least one {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card played before it to have an effect, meaning that {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} will have consumed any {{BD|Vigor}} that came from {{R|Akabeko}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 24: Potions?!'''\n** Finisher card description:\"You have played 2 Attacks.\" -> \"2 Attacks played.\"\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Fixed a rare crash with Finisher card.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2290":{"pageid":2290,"ns":0,"title":"Flying Sleeves","revisions":[{"revid":55788,"parentid":50645,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Flying Sleeves\n|Image       = Purple-FlyingSleeves.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Deal (4;6) damage twice.\n}}\n{{C|Flying Sleeves}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (6 if upgraded) damage twice. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits 2 times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2286":{"pageid":2286,"ns":0,"title":"Foresight","revisions":[{"revid":55791,"parentid":50664,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Foresight\n|Image       = Purple-Foresight.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the start of your turn, {{KW|Scry}} (3;4).\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Foresight}} {{Keyword Infobox|Scry}}\n{{C|Foresight}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Foresight}}, which allows you to {{KW|Scry}} that amount at the start of every turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have {{R|Golden Eye}}, you will be able to {{KW|Scry}} 2 more cards.\n* {{BD|Foresight}} will reliably activate {{C|Nirvana}}.\n* As it allows you to {{KW|Scry}}, any {{C|Weave}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand. \n** If a {{C|Weave}} is among the cards {{KW|Scry|Scryed}} by {{C|Foresight}} and is discarded this way, it will immediately be brought back into your hand.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2135":{"pageid":2135,"ns":0,"title":"Heatsinks","revisions":[{"revid":55815,"parentid":50594,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Heatsinks\n|Image       = Blue-Heatsinks.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you play a Power card, draw (1;2) (card;cards).\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Heatsink}}{{C|Heatsinks}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Heatsink}}, which allows you to draw that amount of cards whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If it is played twice using {{C|Amplify}}, {{C|Echo Form}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, the first play will already draw cards as a result of the second play.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with all other {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards, as well as itself, meaning it also synergizes with {{C|Amplify}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2470":{"pageid":2470,"ns":0,"title":"Mind Blast","revisions":[{"revid":55862,"parentid":50733,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Mind Blast\n|Image       = Colorless-MindBlast.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|CostPlus    = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Innate}}.<br>Deal damage equal to the number of cards in your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Innate}}\n{{C|Mind Blast}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals damage equal to the number of cards in your draw pile. It has {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always be in the first hand of combat.\n\n== Obtaining Mind Blast ==\n{{C|Mind Blast}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As this {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card is {{KW|Innate}}, it guarantees that it will be able to benefit from the {{BD|Vulnerable}} applied by {{R|Bag of Marbles}} and the temporary {{BD|Strength}} gained from {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}.\n\n* It synergizes with cards that increase the amount of cards in your draw pile:\n** {{C|Reboot}} or {{C|Deep Breath}} will shuffle your discard pile into your draw pile.\n** Cards such as {{C|Chrysalis}} and {{C|Wild Strike}} will increase the amount of cards in your draw pile.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Mind Blast card now correctly works with Controlled Chaos mod.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Mind Blast is now always Innate and costs 2. Upgrade reduces cost to 1. (previously upgraded to Innate, always cost 0)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Mind Blast now shows you how much damage it will deal on the card itself.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** MindBlast+. Gains Innate.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Fixed rare crash for MindBlastAction.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Adding Laser Beam VFX to MindBlast card.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1852":{"pageid":1852,"ns":0,"title":"Phantasmal Killer","revisions":[{"revid":55894,"parentid":50540,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Phantasmal Killer\n|Image       = Green-PhantasmalKiller.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Next turn, your Attacks deal double damage.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Phantasmal}}{{Power Infobox|Double Damage}}\n{{C|Phantasmal Killer}} is a 1 (0) {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\nIt applies the {{BD|Phantasmal}} [[Buff]] on the player, which will wear off at the start of the player's next turn and apply the {{BD|Double Damage}} buff, doubling all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attack}} damage during that turn. This [[Buff]] wears off at the start of the next turn. Only one stack of {{BD|Phantasmal}} will be lost each turn, meaning the player will gain {{BD|Double Damage}} for as many turns as they have stacks of {{BD|Phantasmal}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Double Damage}} will multiply with other buffs/debuffs that multiply damage (e.g. 1.5 multiplier from {{BD|Vulnerable}} with 2 multiplier from {{BD|Double Damage}} will deal triple damage).\n** {{C|Terror}} and other sources of {{BD|Vulnerable}}\n** {{R|Pen Nib}}\n\n* {{KW|Retain}} effects allow attacks to be saved for the turn the player gains {{BD|Double Damage}}\n** {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}\n** {{C|Equilibrium}}\n** {{R|Runic Pyramid}}\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Any non-attack sources of damage are not doubled, such as:\n** {{BD|Poison}}\n** Damage [[Relics]] like {{R|Letter Opener}}\n** [[Buffs]] such as {{BD|Thorns}} from {{C|Caltrops}} or {{R|Bronze Scales}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Phantasmal Killer card buffed. Cost reduced from 2 -> 1.\n** Phantasmal Killer+ card buffed. Cost reduced from 1 -> 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Phantasmal Killer power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Pen Nib and Double Damage (Phantasmal Killer) now stack as they're separate powers.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Phantasmal Killer now correctly stacks.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2085":{"pageid":2085,"ns":0,"title":"Rainbow","revisions":[{"revid":55913,"parentid":50626,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Rainbow\n|Image       = Blue-Rainbow.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Lightning}}.<br>{{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}}.<br>{{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Dark}}.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Frost}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Dark}}\n{{C|Rainbow}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. <!---When played, it {{KW|Channel|Channels}} a {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}}, a {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}}, and a {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}}, in that order, and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} (doesn't Exhaust).--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}, and Rainbow is one of the only cards which can produce multiple different Orb types. Moreover, unlike {{C|Chaos}}, Rainbow will always produce three different Orb types, and so will cause {{C|Compile Driver}} to draw at least three cards in general.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Rainbow works best with other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, allowing Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} more frequently. <!--- No idea what to include as prototypical orb gen cards, so just went with these two--->\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of the Orbs generated by Rainbow: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n* Some Orb types have individual synergies:\n** {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n** {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits an additional time for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n** {{C|Blizzard}} does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n** {{C|Darkness|Darkness+}} triggers all {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb's}} [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] an additional time.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Orbs generated by Rainbow less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Adding VFX for Rainbow card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** If cards have too many keywords (eg Rainbow), the tips are shifted up.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2073":{"pageid":2073,"ns":0,"title":"Rebound","revisions":[{"revid":56094,"parentid":55916,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Rebound\n|Image       = Blue-Rebound.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (9;12) damage.<br>Put the next card you play this turn on top of your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Rebound}}\n{{C|Rebound}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (12 if upgraded) damage, and gives you one {{BD|Rebound}}, which will place the next card that is played on top of your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Rebound}} takes effect after the {{BD|Rebound|Rebounded}} card is fully resolved, meaning cards that draw will not draw themselves, but be placed on top of the draw pile after.\n\n* Although {{C|Mayhem}} plays the top card of the draw pile, it cannot be used in tandem with {{C|Rebound}} to play a specific card, as {{C|Mayhem}} activates after cards are drawn at the start of your turn, meaning the {{BD|Rebound|Rebounded}} card will already be in hand.\n** This could still be achieved if you {{BD|Rebound|Rebounded}} more cards than you draw at the start of your turn. \n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Cards that cannot be placed back on top of the draw pile when played, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} and cards that {{KW|Exhaust}} will still consume {{BD|Rebound}}, even though it will have no effect.\n\n* Theoretically, {{BD|Rebound}} can stack, but in practice 1 is the highest you can achieve, as playing {{C|Rebound}} will consume any {{BD|Rebound}} that is already active. Even playing it multiple times using {{C|Echo Form}}, {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}} will result in the first {{BD|Rebound}} being consumed.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Rebound card not working with Strange Spoon relic.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Rebound card no longer puts Burns on top of your deck.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Rebound card buff: Damage 8 -> 9. Upgraded 11 -> 12.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2074":{"pageid":2074,"ns":0,"title":"Recursion","revisions":[{"revid":50566,"parentid":50565,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Recursion\n|Image       = Blue-Recursion.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Evoke}} your next Orb.<br>{{KW|Channel}} the Orb that was just {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}.\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Evoke}} {{Keyword Infobox|Channel}}\n{{C|Recursion}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Recursion}} will actually {{KW|Channel}} the exact [[Orb]] it {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}, so any built up damage from a {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}} will be carried over.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2421":{"pageid":2421,"ns":0,"title":"Sands of Time","revisions":[{"revid":54864,"parentid":50679,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sands of Time\n|Image       = Purple-SandsofTime.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 4\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}.<br>Deal (20;26) damage.<br>When {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, lower its cost by 1 this combat.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}}\n{{C|Sands of Time}} is a 4 {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 20 (26 if upgraded) damage. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn, and it will lower its {{Icon|PE}}-cost by 1 whenever it is {{KW|Retain|Retained}} at the end of your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"2023":{"pageid":2023,"ns":0,"title":"Slice","revisions":[{"revid":50490,"parentid":36299,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Slice\n|Image       = Green-Slice.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (6;9) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Slice}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (9 if upgraded) damage.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of this card by 4.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Slice card buffed. Damage increased from 5 -> 6.\n** Slice+ card buffed. Damage increased from 8 -> 9.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2271":{"pageid":2271,"ns":0,"title":"Tantrum","revisions":[{"revid":55970,"parentid":54865,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Tantrum\n|Image       = Purple-Tantrum.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal 3 damage (3;4) times.<br>Enter {{KW|Wrath}}.<br>Shuffle this card into your draw pile.\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Wrath}}\n{{C|Tantrum}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 3 damage 3 times (4 times if upgraded) and makes you enter the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Tantrum}} first deals damage and only then makes you enter {{KW|Wrath}}, meaning its own damage is not yet doubled if you were not already in {{KW|Wrath}}. \n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits three (four if upgraded) times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* When entering {{KW|Wrath}} if you are not in {{KW|Wrath}} yet:\n** If you have {{BD|Rushdown}} from {{C|Rushdown}}, you will draw that many cards.\n** You will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n*** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n*** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n*** If you were in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} before, you will gain 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''', or 3 if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Wrath}} changes the effects of some cards:\n** {{C|Halt}} will give its additional {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Indignation}} will apply {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* While in {{KW|Wrath}}, all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage you deal is doubled, but you also take double damage from enemy attacks.{{KW|Wrath}} only doubles damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, not from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{KW|Wrath}} is worse than the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}} in every way except for the aformentioned ones, using {{C|Tantrum}} while in {{KW|Divinity}} is generally bad, if it does not end combat.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}